.TH ISSUE 1 "September 2026" "SPP CLI Manual" "SPP System Documentation"
.SH NAME
issue \- Manage SPPDocs project issues from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B php spp.php issue
\fIaction\fR
[\fB\-\-project\fR=\fIproject-id\fR]
[\fB\-\-title\fR=\fItitle\fR]
[\fB\-\-id\fR=\fInumber\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B issue
enables terminal developers to list, inspect, create, and close issues stored in SPPDocs projects without leaving the command line.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B list
Display a formatted table of issues for the specified project.
.TP
.B create
Create a new issue. Requires \-\-title.
.TP
.B view
Display detailed attributes, description, and metadata of an issue. Requires \-\-id.
.TP
.B close
Mark an issue as closed and append a closing comment. Requires \-\-id.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-project= "project-id"
Target project. Defaults to demo-app.
.TP
.BI \-\-id= "number"
Sequential issue number (#1) or ID string.
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
Resolves StorageFactory, writes to index cache or SQLite WAL tables, and invokes workflow transitions.
